  "notes": "Source: official 2026-2027 University of Colorado Boulder undergraduate catalog page 'Business Administration - Bachelor of Science (BSBA)' (Leeds School of Business). Transcribed from the catalog's 'Recommended Four-Year Plan of Study' grid, cross-checked against the catalog-generated program PDF for row labels the HTML grid drops in upper years. Plan total 120.5 credit hours matches the catalog's published plan total of 120.5 (minimum degree requirement is 120: Business core 30 + area of emphasis 18 + business electives 16 + General Education 33 + non-business electives 23). Students must complete an area of emphasis (min 18 hours) in one of ten areas: accounting, business analytics, finance, management, management information systems, marketing, real estate, strategy & entrepreneurship, supply chain management, sustainable business. QUIRK (documented, not guessed): the catalog's Year Four Fall grid lists a semester total of 15 credit hours but text extraction of the program PDF shows only 4 labeled rows (12 cr); the missing 3-credit row is determined by the degree category totals — General Education (33), business core (30), emphasis (18), and business electives (16 incl. BADM courses) are all fully accounted for elsewhere in the grid, leaving non-business electives at 20 of the required 23, so the missing row is recorded as a non-business elective (3 cr). BCOR 1015 and BCOR 1030: the grid lists them as alternates in both Year One semesters; the degree requires both (3 + 3 = 6 toward the 30-hour business core), so they are recorded one per semester with the alternate noted. BADM 1250/1260/2010 (fractional 1.5/2/1 credits) count toward the 16 business-elective hours, which is why the recommended plan totals 120.5 rather than 120.",
